---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
// Angka dan pilihan hukum di bawah (masa penerimaan 10 hari kerja, garansi perbaikan 30 hari, bunga
// keterlambatan, batas tanggung jawab, hukum New York) adalah nilai awal; tinjau bersama penasihat hukum.
---
<LegalLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions"
  description="The terms that apply when you work with Magiapix or use the Magiapix website."
  updated="November 19, 2026"
  intro="These terms govern every project Magiapix delivers and every visit to this website. Please read them carefully. By signing a proposal, paying an invoice or using this site, you accept them."
>
  <h2>Definitions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>“Magiapix”, “we”, “us”</strong> means the Magiapix studio, {SITE.address.join(', ')}.</li>
    <li><strong>“Client”, “you”</strong> means the person or company that accepts a Proposal or uses our Services.</li>
    <li><strong>“Proposal”</strong> means the written quote, statement of work or estimate that describes a Project, its Deliverables, timeline and fees.</li>
    <li><strong>“Project”</strong> means the work described in an accepted Proposal.</li>
    <li><strong>“Services”</strong> means web design, web development, web apps, brand visualization and related work.</li>
    <li><strong>“Deliverables”</strong> means the final files, designs, code and other results we hand over under a Proposal.</li>
    <li><strong>“Client Materials”</strong> means text, images, logos, data, accounts and any other content you give us.</li>
    <li><strong>“Business day”</strong> means Monday to Friday, excluding public holidays in New York.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Agreement and order of priority</h2>
  <p>A Project starts only when you accept a Proposal in writing (email is enough) and we receive the deposit.</p>
  <p>Each accepted Proposal and these terms together form the agreement between you and Magiapix. If they conflict, the Proposal applies for that Project. If a signed contract exists, the signed contract applies first.</p>
  <p>Your own purchase-order terms or general conditions do not apply, unless we accept them in writing.</p>
  <p>A Proposal is valid for 30 days from its date, unless it states another period.</p>

  <h2>Scope of work</h2>
  <p>We deliver only what the Proposal lists. Anything not listed is out of scope.</p>
  <p>Unless the Proposal says otherwise, the following are not included:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>copywriting, translation, photography and video production;</li>
    <li>purchase of stock images, fonts, plugins, domains or software licences;</li>
    <li>hosting fees, ongoing maintenance, security updates and support after the warranty period;</li>
    <li>search-engine ranking, advertising results or any specific business outcome;</li>
    <li>legal review of your content, including privacy notices, cookie banners and terms for your own site.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Change requests</h2>
  <p>You can ask for changes at any time. For every out-of-scope request, we tell you in writing what it adds to the fee and the timeline.</p>
  <p>We start out-of-scope work only after you approve that estimate in writing. Approved changes become part of the Project.</p>

  <h2>Fees, invoices and payment</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Fees are stated in the Proposal. They exclude taxes, which we add where the law requires.</li>
    <li>Unless the Proposal says otherwise, we invoice a 50% deposit before work starts and the balance in milestones or on completion.</li>
    <li>Invoices are due within 14 days of the invoice date.</li>
    <li>You pay all bank and transfer charges, so that we receive the full invoiced amount.</li>
    <li>Third-party costs that you approve, such as licences or hosting, are billed at cost or paid by you directly.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If an invoice is more than 14 days overdue, we may pause all work until it is paid. The timeline moves by at least the length of the pause.</p>
  <p>Overdue amounts carry interest of 1% per month, or the highest rate the law allows if that is lower.</p>
  <p>If you dispute an invoice, tell us in writing within 7 days of receiving it and pay the part that is not in dispute.</p>

  <h2>Timelines and delays</h2>
  <p>The Proposal gives a planned timeline. It depends on you supplying Client Materials, feedback and approvals on the dates we agree.</p>
  <p>If your input is late, every later date moves by at least the same time. We may also need to reschedule the Project around our other commitments.</p>
  <p>If a Project is on hold because of you for more than 30 days, we may invoice all work completed so far. Restarting the Project may require a new schedule and, where costs have changed, a revised fee.</p>

  <h2>Feedback and revisions</h2>
  <p>The Proposal states how many revision rounds each stage includes. One round means one consolidated list of changes from you, sent in writing.</p>
  <p>Changes to work you have already approved, or new directions after approval, count as change requests. Extra rounds are billed at our current hourly rate.</p>
  <p>Please name one person on your side who collects feedback and gives approvals. We may treat their instructions as yours.</p>

  <h2>Acceptance of deliverables</h2>
  <p>When we deliver a stage or the final Deliverables, you have 10 business days to approve them or to report, in writing, where they do not match the Proposal.</p>
  <p>We fix reported non-conformities within a reasonable time and deliver again for review.</p>
  <p>Deliverables count as accepted when you approve them, when the 10 days pass without a written report, or when you publish or use them, whichever comes first.</p>

  <h2>Your responsibilities</h2>
  <p>You agree to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>give us accurate and complete information about your business and the Project;</li>
    <li>supply Client Materials, access and approvals on the agreed dates;</li>
    <li>review work promptly and keep a single point of contact;</li>
    <li>check all final content, including prices, claims and legal text, before it goes live;</li>
    <li>keep your own backups and the passwords for accounts we set up for you.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Client materials and warranties</h2>
  <p>You confirm that you own, or have permission to use, all Client Materials. You also confirm that they do not break any law or anyone else’s rights, including copyright, trademark and privacy rights.</p>
  <p>You are responsible for the content you publish on the Deliverables, and for meeting the laws that apply to your business and your website.</p>
  <p>You will compensate Magiapix for claims, losses and reasonable legal costs that arise because Client Materials, or your use of the Deliverables, infringe someone’s rights or break the law.</p>

  <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
  <p><strong>Ownership on payment.</strong> When we receive full payment for a Project, we transfer to you the rights in the final Deliverables that were created for you. Until then, we own them and you may not use them in public.</p>
  <p><strong>Our tools stay ours.</strong> We keep all rights in our pre-existing know-how, code libraries, components, templates and tools, even when they are part of a Deliverable. You receive a permanent, non-exclusive licence to use them as part of that Deliverable.</p>
  <p><strong>Drafts and concepts.</strong> Unused concepts, drafts and source working files stay our property, unless the Proposal includes them.</p>
  <p><strong>Third-party assets.</strong> Fonts, stock media, plugins and open-source software stay subject to their own licences. We tell you which ones the Deliverables use. Where a paid licence is needed, it must be in your name, and you keep it active.</p>

  <h2>Portfolio and credit</h2>
  <p>We may show the finished work, and the fact that we worked with you, in our portfolio, case studies, social media and award entries.</p>
  <p>We never publish your confidential information. If you need the work kept private, tell us before the Project starts, and we will agree on that in the Proposal.</p>
  <p>We may place a small “Site by Magiapix” credit in the website footer. You can ask us to remove it.</p>

  <h2>Confidentiality</h2>
  <p>Each party keeps the other party’s non-public business information confidential. Each party uses it only for the Project.</p>
  <p>This duty does not cover information that is public, that the receiving party already had or developed independently, or that the law requires it to disclose.</p>
  <p>This duty lasts for 3 years after the Project ends.</p>

  <h2>Warranty and bug fixes</h2>
  <p>For 30 days after final acceptance, we fix free of charge any defect that stops the Deliverables from working as the Proposal describes.</p>
  <p>This warranty does not cover problems caused by:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>changes made by you or anyone other than Magiapix;</li>
    <li>third-party services, hosting, plugins or browser and operating-system updates released after delivery;</li>
    <li>use of the Deliverables in a way the Proposal did not describe.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Except for this warranty, we deliver our Services and Deliverables “as is”. We do not promise any specific result, such as traffic, rankings, sales or uninterrupted availability.</p>

  <h2>Hosting, maintenance and third-party services</h2>
  <p>Deliverables often run on outside services, such as hosting, domain registrars, content-management systems and payment or analytics tools. Those services are governed by their own terms between you and the provider.</p>
  <p>We are not responsible for their outages, price changes, policy changes or data loss.</p>
  <p>Maintenance, updates and support after the warranty period are only included when they are part of a separate maintenance agreement.</p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>Neither party is liable for indirect or consequential loss, including lost profits, lost revenue, lost data or damage to reputation.</p>
  <p>Our total liability for any Project is limited to the fees you paid us for that Project in the 12 months before the claim.</p>
  <p>Nothing in these terms limits liability that the law does not allow to be limited, such as liability for fraud or gross negligence.</p>

  <h2>Termination and cancellation</h2>
  <p><strong>By you.</strong> You may cancel a Project at any time with written notice. You then pay for all work completed up to the notice date and for any committed third-party costs. The deposit is not refundable.</p>
  <p><strong>By us.</strong> We may end a Project with written notice if an invoice is more than 30 days overdue, if you seriously break these terms, or if you ask us to do something unlawful or unethical.</p>
  <p><strong>On termination.</strong> We hand over the work paid for at that date. Ownership of unpaid work stays with us.</p>
  <p>Sections on payment, intellectual property, confidentiality, liability and disputes remain in force after a Project ends.</p>

  <h2>Force majeure</h2>
  <p>Neither party is responsible for a delay or failure caused by events beyond its reasonable control. Examples are natural disasters, war, epidemics, government action, power or internet outages, and failures of major platforms.</p>
  <p>The affected party tells the other party promptly and resumes work as soon as possible. If such an event lasts more than 60 days, either party may end the Project by written notice. Work done until then is paid for.</p>

  <h2>Non-solicitation</h2>
  <p>During a Project and for 12 months after it ends, you agree not to hire, or engage directly, a Magiapix employee or contractor who worked on your Project, unless we agree in writing.</p>

  <h2>Use of this website</h2>
  <p>The content of this website is for general information only. It is not an offer, and it is not professional advice.</p>
  <p>Content created by Magiapix, including our text, design, code and our name and logo, belongs to Magiapix. Other content belongs to its respective owners, as explained in the next section. You may not copy or reuse any of it without permission from the owner.</p>
  <p>Do not try to disrupt the site, gain unauthorised access, or collect its data automatically.</p>
  <p>Links to other websites are for convenience. We do not control those websites and are not responsible for them.</p>
  <p>How we handle personal data is described in our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>Showcase content and ownership</h2>
  <p>The projects on this website show the kind of work Magiapix can design and build. They are a demonstration of our capabilities. They are not all commissioned client work, and a project page is not a statement that the named brand hired us.</p>
  <p>Some projects are placeholders. They hold a place in our portfolio until we can publish real client work, which confidentiality agreements often prevent. A placeholder may later be replaced, changed or removed without notice.</p>
  <p>Some content on this website is not owned by Magiapix, either in full or in part. This includes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>AI-generated media.</strong> Images, video and other assets made fully or partly with generative AI tools. Such material may not be protected by copyright, and we do not claim exclusive ownership of it.</li>
    <li><strong>Studies and recreations.</strong> Concepts that rebuild, reinterpret or reverse-engineer the design or behaviour of existing websites and products, made to study and demonstrate techniques.</li>
    <li><strong>Third-party material.</strong> Stock photography, fonts, icons, video, open-source code and screenshots of third-party websites, used under their own licences or as references.</li>
    <li><strong>Names and marks.</strong> Brand names, logos and trademarks of other companies. These belong to their owners. Their use does not mean those owners endorse, sponsor or work with Magiapix.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Client names, quotes, figures and results on project pages may be illustrative examples rather than reports of real engagements.</p>
  <p>We claim rights only in the parts that Magiapix created itself, such as our own design, layout and code. We do not claim ownership of the material listed above, and you may not reuse it based on this website.</p>
  <p>If you own content shown here and want it credited, changed or removed, email us at <a href={SITE.emailHref}>{SITE.email}</a>. We will respond promptly.</p>

  <h2>Independent parties</h2>
  <p>Magiapix works as an independent contractor. Nothing in these terms creates a partnership, joint venture or employment relationship.</p>
  <p>We may use qualified subcontractors. We remain responsible for their work.</p>

  <h2>Notices</h2>
  <p>Formal notices under these terms must be in writing. Email counts as writing. Send them to the address in the Proposal, or to <a href={SITE.emailHref}>{SITE.email}</a> for Magiapix.</p>
  <p>A notice takes effect on the business day after it is sent.</p>

  <h2>Governing law and disputes</h2>
  <p>These terms and every Project are governed by the laws of the State of New York, USA, without regard to its conflict-of-law rules.</p>
  <p>If a dispute arises, both parties first try in good faith to settle it by negotiation for 30 days, starting from a written notice that describes the dispute.</p>
  <p>If the dispute is not settled, the state and federal courts located in New York County, New York, have exclusive jurisdiction.</p>

  <h2>General</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Entire agreement.</strong> These terms and the Proposal are the complete agreement for a Project. They replace earlier discussions about that Project.</li>
    <li><strong>Severability.</strong> If a court finds any part of these terms invalid, that part is limited as little as possible, and the rest stays in force.</li>
    <li><strong>No waiver.</strong> If we do not enforce a right at once, we do not give it up.</li>
    <li><strong>Assignment.</strong> You may not transfer your rights or duties under these terms without our written consent.</li>
    <li><strong>Language.</strong> These terms are written in English. If they are translated, the English version prevails.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms. The date at the top of this page shows the current version.</p>
  <p>Changes do not affect a Project that is already under way. That Project keeps the terms that applied when you accepted its Proposal, unless both parties agree otherwise in writing.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about these terms? Write to us at <a href={SITE.emailHref}>{SITE.email}</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
